ng to nail anything down I make  it an enjoyable exploration of the  language and if we do that then we'll  want to continue we may want to continue  to improve in length in one language or  we may decide that even though we are  less than perfect in language a we want  to explore language B and we may go back  to language aid so it should always be a  pleasurable voyage of discovery and we  can all learn there's no such thing as a  special talent for language learning  people in some countries like countries  where the language their language is not  widely spoken Finland  Liston Stein Holland they tend to be  better at learning languages because  they have a better attitude so language  learning is not about talent we all  learn our first language we can all  learn more languages it's about attitude  so I encourage you to take away from the  this sort of 12 lesson course that it's  important to be confident that you can  learn the language try to find things  that you enjoy in terms of content in  terms of activity do things that you  enjoy and then feel confident that the  kind of language learning activity  you're engaged in is going to help you  don't second-guess what you're doing why  am i studying this way don't  second-guess why you're even spending  time with the language if you are  convinced that it is something you want  to do and you are convinced that it is  that you're using a method that's  effective and if you feel that you will  eventually learn the language even  though it takes a long time you know  it's not a 100-yard dash it's a long  distance run you will eventually get  there and perhaps develop an attitude  towards language learning that stays  with you  your life so thank you for listening and  good luck in your language learning  activities bye for now
 

